          "solution": {
            "en": "For $T=1$ year, compound interest equals simple interest: $CI = \\dfrac{PR}{100}$, so $12=\\dfrac{100\\times R}{100}=R$. Thus $R=12\\%$.",
            "ne": "$T=1$ वर्षका लागि, चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज साधारण ब्याज बराबर हुन्छ: $CI = \\dfrac{PR}{100}$, त्यसैले $12=\\dfrac{100\\times R}{100}=R$। त्यसैले $R=12\\%$।"
          }
        },
        {
          "partId": "ex2.1-q4-b",
          "solution": {
            "en": "$CI = P\\left[\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^T-1\\right]$: $42 = 200\\left[\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^2-1\\right]$, so $\\dfrac{42}{200}=0.21=\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^2-1$, giving $\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^2=1.21$, so $1+\\dfrac{R}{100}=1.1$, i.e. $R=10\\%$.",
            "ne": "$CI = P\\left[\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^T-1\\right]$: $42 = 200\\left[\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^2-1\\right]$, त्यसैले $\\dfrac{42}{200}=0.21=\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^2-1$, जसबाट $\\left(1+\\dfrac{R}{100}\\right)^2=1.21$, त्यसैले $1+\\dfrac{R}{100}=1.1$, अर्थात् $R=10\\%$।"
          }
        }
      ]
